インポートされていること\n+\t\texpect(formContainer).toMatch(\n+\t\t\t/import\\s+{[^}]*useActionState[^}]*}\\s+from\\s+[\"']react[\"']/\n+\t\t);\n \t});\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@__tests__/migration/react19-compat.test.ts` around lines 14 - 25, The test\ncurrently checks only that \"useActionState\" exists and that there's an import\nfrom \"react\" but doesn't assert that \"useActionState\" is actually imported from\n\"react\"; update the assertion in the test that reads FormContainer.tsx (used in\nthe it block named \"useActionState が react からインポートされていること\") to explicitly verify\na named import of useActionState from \"react\" (e.g., assert the file matches a\nregex that looks for import { ... useActionState ... } from 'react' such as\nmatching \"import\" with a named specifier containing useActionState followed by\nfrom 'react') so the test ensures the symbol useActionState is imported from\nreact rather than merely present or imported from react-dom.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits b33297c to f3ecba8","created_at":"2026-03-09T15:40:59Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T16:34:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255002","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255002"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255002"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255002/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_lin