ory: myoshi2891/Next-Store\n\nLength of output: 92\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find FormContainer.tsx and check actionFunction type definition\nfd \"FormContainer.tsx\" -x cat -n {}\n```\n\nRepository: myoshi2891/Next-Store\n\nLength of output: 935\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for .bind() usages with proper file type handling\nrg -n '\\.bind\\(null,' --glob='*.tsx' --glob='*.ts' -C2 | head -100\n```\n\nRepository: myoshi2891/Next-Store\n\nLength of output: 1087\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find the specific action functions mentioned in the review\nfd \"deleteProductAction\" -x cat -n {}\nfd \"deleteReviewAction\" -x cat -n {}\nfd \"toggleFavoriteAction\" -x cat -n {}\n```\n\nRepository: myoshi2891/Next-Store\n\nLength of output: 47\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if these files exist and examine them\nfd -e tsx -e ts | grep -E \"(deleteProduct|deleteReview|toggleFavorite|FavoriteToggle)\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: myoshi2891/Next-Store\n\nLength of output: 152\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find the actionFunction type definition\nfd \"types.ts\" -path \"*/utils/*\" -x cat -n {}\n```\n\nRepository: myoshi2891/Next-Store\n\nLength of output: 233\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find and check the action function definitions\nfd -e ts -e tsx -path \"*\" | xargs grep -l \"deleteProductAction\\|deleteReviewAction\\|toggleFavoriteAction\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: myoshi2891/Next-Store\n\nLength of output: 233\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for these action function declarations\nrg \"export.*deleteProductAction|export.*deleteReviewAction|export.*toggleFavoriteAction\" -A 3\n```\n\nRepository: myoshi2891/Next-Store\n\nLength of output: 1948\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find utils/types.ts or similar\nfd \"types.ts\" | grep utils\n```\n\nRepository: myoshi2891/Next-Store\n\nLength of output: 79\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find actionFunction type definition\nrg \"actionFunction\" --type-add 'ts:*.ts' --type-add 'tsx:*.tsx' -A 3 -B 1\n```\n\nRepository: myoshi2891/Next-Store\n\nLength of output: 6126\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**`actionFunction` 型と実装されたアクション関数の署名が互換性を失っています。**\n\n`actionFunction` 型は `prevState: { message: string }` を要求しますが、以下のアクション関数は異なる形状のオブジェクトを期待しています：\n\n- `deleteProductAction` は `prevState: { productId: string }` を要求\n- `deleteReviewAction` は `prevState: { reviewId: string }` を要求  \n- `toggleFavoriteAction` は `prevState: { productId: string; favoriteId: string | null; pathname: string; }` を要求\n\nこれらを `.bind()` で部分適用してもFormContainerに渡すと、型チェックが失敗し、実行時に状態管理が機能しなくなります。アクション関数の署名を統一するか、FormContainerの型定義を調整する必要があります。\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@components/form/FormContainer.tsx` at line 15, The FormContainer's\nactionFunction type is incompatible with the actual action implementations\n(deleteProductAction, deleteReviewAction, toggleFavoriteAction) because each\nexpects a different prevState shape; update the typing so FormContainer accepts\na generic action signature instead of fixed prevState: { message: string }.\nConcretely, change the action prop/type alias (actionFunction) to be generic\n(e.g., actionFunction<TPrev>) or to accept a union/unknown prevState (e.g.,\n(prevState: TPrev) => Promise<any> or (prevState: unknown) => Promise<any>),\nthen update FormContainer to be generic over that PrevState and propagate the\ngeneric to its callers, or alternatively define a discriminated union of the\nspecific prevState shapes matching deleteProductAction, deleteReviewAction, and\ntoggleFavoriteAction so all implementations satisfy the action prop. Ensure\nreferences to actionFunction, FormContainer, deleteProductAction,\ndeleteReviewAction, and toggleFavoriteAction are updated accordingly so type\nchecking remains strict and runtime behavior is preserved.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-09T15:40:59Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T02:14:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255015","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255015"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255015"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255015/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":15,"original_line":15,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":10,"position":10,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255029","pull_request_review_id":3916334651,"id":2906255029,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDONvrgrc6tOe61","diff_hunk":"@@ -11,12 +11,12 @@ import Link from \"next/link\";\n import { Button } from \"../ui/button\";\n import { links } from \"@/utils/links\";\n import UserIcon from \"./UserIcon\";\n-import { SignedIn, SignedOut, SignInButton, SignUpButton } from \"@clerk/nextjs\";\n+import { Show, SignInButton, SignUpButton } from \"@clerk/nextjs\";\n import SignOutLink from \"./SignOutLink\";\n import { auth } from \"@clerk/nextjs/server\";\n \n-function LinksDropdown() {\n-\tconst { userId } = auth();\n+async function LinksDropdown() {\n+\tconst { userId } = await auth();\n \tconst isAdmin = userId === process.env.ADMIN_USER_ID;","path":"components/navbar/LinksDropdown.tsx","commit_id":"f27220ad6e86838597f6c40637e4d585ffc8afe6","original_commit_id":"a2e66ac88626f39cced1ccb671e4d54703f58e2f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🧹 Nitpick_ | _🔵 Trivial_\n\n**サーバーサイドとクライアントサイドの認証状態の混在に注意してください。**\n\n`isAdmin` の判定はサーバーサイドの `await auth()` で行われていますが、`Show when=\"signed-in\"` 内でこの値を使用しています。`Show` コンポーネントはクライアントサイドで認証状態を再評価するため、サーバーレンダリング時とクライアントハイドレーション時で一貫性が保たれることを確認してください。\n\n現在の実装自体は動作しますが、理解しておくべきポイントです。\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 48-60\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@components/navbar/LinksDropdown.tsx` around lines 18 - 20, LinksDropdown\ncurrently computes isAdmin using server-side await auth() but then uses it\ninside the client-evaluated Show component, risking SSR/rehydration mismatch;\nfix by keeping admin-checking on the same runtime as Show — either move the\nadmin check into a client component (convert LinksDropdown or the dropdown\nfragment to a client component and use a client-side auth/session hook to\ncompute isAdmin) or keep LinksDropdown server-only and stop using the\nserver-derived isAdmin inside Show (instead pass a stable serialized prop or\nrender admin-only markup server-side); refer to LinksDropdown, isAdmin, auth(),\nand the Show component to locate and change the logic so the admin flag is\ncomputed and consumed on the same side (client or server) to avoid inconsistent\nauth state.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits b33297c to c7fc0b2","created_at":"2026-03-09T15:40:59Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T01:25:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255029","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255029"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255029"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255029/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":18,"original_start_line":18,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":20,"original_line":20,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":13,"position":13,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255036","pull_request_review_id":3916334651,"id":2906255036,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDONvrgrc6tOe68","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,6 +1,9 @@\n /** @type {import('next').NextConfig} */\n const nextConfig = {\n \timages: {\n+\t\t// NAT64 環境で Cloudflare CDN (Supabase) の IPv6 アドレスが\n+\t\t// RFC 6052 (64:ff9b::/96) に該当し \"private IP\" と判定されるため有効化\n+\t\tdangerouslyAllowLocalIP: true,","path":"next.config.mjs","commit_id":"f3ecba86a341d4855b252948432186adcab817b6","original_commit_id":"a2e66ac88626f39cced1ccb671e4d54703f58e2f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Next.js dangerouslyAllowLocalIP security implications`\n\n💡 Result:\n\n`images.dangerouslyAllowLocalIP` (Next.js Image Optimization) removes Next’s default block on fetching/optimizing images from **local/private IP ranges** (e.g., `127.0.0.1`, `10.0.0.0/8`, `192.168.0.0/16`). Next.js explicitly warns it’s “not recommended for most users” because it “could allow malicious users to access content on your internal network.” [1]\n\n### Security implications (why it’s risky)\n- **SSRF / internal network reachability:** If an attacker can influence any image URL that gets routed through `/_next/image` (directly or indirectly), enabling local IPs can let them coerce your server into making requests to **internal-only services** (admin panels, metadata endpoints, Redis, etc.) and potentially exfiltrate responses (classic SSRF pattern). [1]\n- **Expanded blast radius when allowlists are broad:** Misconfigurations that allow arbitrary upstream URLs (e.g., overly broad patterns) make SSRF-style abuse more feasible; security guidance around `/_next/image` commonly emphasizes strict allowlisting for this reason. [2][3]\n\n### Practical guidance\n- Keep `dangerouslyAllowLocalIP: false` unless you *truly* need to optimize images hosted on private IPs. [1]\n- If you enable it, treat it like an SSRF-sensitive feature:\n  - Ensure image `src` values are **not user-controlled** (or are heavily validated).\n  - Use **tight** `remotePatterns`/`localPatterns` (avoid wildcards; restrict pathname and query where possible).\n  - Consider network controls (firewall, allow egress only to required hosts) around the Next.js server.\n\n**Sources:** Next.js docs on `dangerouslyAllowLocalIP` and its warning [1]; SSRF/abuse discussions around `/_next/image` and the need for strict allowlisting [2][3].  \n\n[1] ([nextjs.org](https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/components/image))  \n[2] ([acunetix.com](https://www.acunetix.com/vulnerabilities/web/next-js-image-blind-ssrf/?utm_source=openai))  \n[3] ([nvd.nist.gov](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-6087?utm_source=openai))\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/components/image\n- 2: https://www.acunetix.com/vulnerabilities/web/next-js-image-blind-ssrf/?utm_source=openai\n- 3: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-6087?utm_source=openai\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**`dangerouslyAllowLocalIP` によるSSRFリスクについて再検討してください。**\n\nこのオプションはプライベートIPアドレスからの画像取得を許可するため、Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) 攻撃のリスクが増加します。Next.jsの公式ドキュメントでは「ほとんどのユーザーには推奨されない」と明記されており、内部ネットワークへのアクセスを許可する可能性があります。\n\n本番環境での使用を再評価し、以下の点を検討してください：\n- Cloudflare/Supabase側の設定やネットワークアーキテクチャで解決できないか\n- 画像URLが確実にユーザーコントロール下にないか（SSRFの要件）\n- `remotePatterns`が十分に厳密か（特にClerkの`/**`パターンは過度に広い可能性）\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@next.config.mjs` around lines 4 - 6, The Next.js config currently enables\ndangerouslyAllowLocalIP which raises SSRF risk; remove or gate this flag (only\nenable in non-production/dev via NODE_ENV) and instead tighten image host\nallowlists in remotePatterns by replacing broad Clerk '/**' patterns with\nexplicit hostnames and strict protocols/ports, add server-side URL validation\n(verify host against allowlist and disallow private IPs after DNS resolution)\nbefore fetching images, and document why/when dangerouslyAllowLocalIP is used so\nproduction builds do not enable it unintentionally.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits b33297c to 1105322","created_at":"2026-03-09T15:40:59Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T02:46:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255036","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255036"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255036"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255036/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":4,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":6,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255047","pull_request_review_id":3916334651,"id":2906255047,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDONvrgrc6tOe7H","diff_hunk":"@@ -6,10 +6,12 @@\n \t\t\"dev\": \"next dev\",\n \t\t\"build\": \"npx prisma generate && next build\",\n \t\t\"start\": \"next start\",\n-\t\t\"lint\": \"next lint\"\n+\t\t\"lint\": \"eslint .\",\n+\t\t\"test\": \"vitest run\",\n+\t\t\"test:watch\": \"vitest\"\n \t},\n \t\"dependencies\": {\n-\t\t\"@clerk/nextjs\": \"^5.1.4\",\n+\t\t\"@clerk/nextjs\": \"^7.0.1\",","path":"package.json","commit_id":"f27220ad6e86838597f6c40637e4d585ffc8afe6","original_commit_id":"a2e66ac88626f39cced1ccb671e4d54703f58e2f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🧹 Nitpick_ | _🔵 Trivial_\n\n**メジャーバージョンアップの動作確認を推奨します。**\n\n以下のメジャーバージョンアップが含まれています：\n- `@clerk/nextjs`: v5 → v7\n- `next`: v14 → v16\n- `react` / `react-dom`: v18 → v19\n\nこれらは breaking changes を含む可能性があります。本 PR 全体での `await auth()` への移行や `useActionState` への変更は、これらのアップグレードに対応したものと理解していますが、テストスイートでの動作確認を十分に行ってください。\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 33-36\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@package.json` at line 14, Package.json bumps major versions for\n`@clerk/nextjs`, next, and react/react-dom which can introduce breaking changes;\nrun comprehensive integration and unit tests across the app and update code to\nmatch new APIs (e.g., ensure auth calls are migrated to await auth() and any\ncomponents/actions using Clerk and Next/React features adopt new patterns such\nas useActionState). Specifically: update usage sites referencing Clerk auth and\nNext/React lifecycle/hooks to the v7/v16/v19 APIs, run the full test suite and\nfix failing tests, and search for symbols like auth(), useActionState,\nClerkProvider/withClerk usages and adjust them to the newer API contracts before\nmerging.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-09T15:40:59Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T02:14:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255047","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255047"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255047"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255047/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":15,"original_line":14,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":11,"position":12,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255054","pull_request_review_id":3916334651,"id":2906255054,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDONvrgrc6tOe7O","diff_hunk":"@@ -43,14 +45,20 @@\n \t},\n \t\"devDependencies\": {\n \t\t\"@faker-js/faker\": \"^9.7.0\",\n+\t\t\"@testing-library/jest-dom\": \"^6.9.1\",\n+\t\t\"@testing-library/react\": \"^16.3.2\",\n+\t\t\"@testing-library/user-event\": \"^14.6.1\",\n \t\t\"@types/node\": \"^20\",\n-\t\t\"@types/react\": \"^18\",\n-\t\t\"@types/react-dom\": \"^18\",\n+\t\t\"@types/react\": \"^19.2.14\",\n+\t\t\"@types/react-dom\": \"^19.2.3\",\n+\t\t\"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^5.1.4\",\n \t\t\"eslint\": \"^8\",\n-\t\t\"eslint-config-next\": \"14.2.3\",\n+\t\t\"eslint-config-next\": \"^16.1.6\",","path":"package.json","commit_id":"f3ecba86a341d4855b252948432186adcab817b6","original_commit_id":"a2e66ac88626f39cced1ccb671e4d54703f58e2f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`eslint-config-next 16 ESLint version compatibility`\n\n💡 Result:\n\n`eslint-config-next` **v16.x** is compatible with **ESLint v9 only**:\n\n- **Peer dependency:** `eslint >= 9.0.0` (so **ESLint 8.x and earlier are not supported**) [1]  \n- **Optional peer dependency:** `typescript >= 3.3.1` [1]\n\nSources: [1] (eslint-config-next 16.1.6 dependency metadata), [2] (Next.js ESLint config docs).\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`eslint-config-next 16 ESLint 8 compatibility error`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nThat “`eslint-config-next@16` + ESLint 8” failure usually happens because the v16 Next.js ESLint setup is built around the **ESLint CLI + flat config** (e.g. `eslint.config.mjs` importing from `eslint/config`), which generally expects **ESLint 9+**. Next.js docs also note that starting with **Next.js 16, `next lint` was removed** in favor of running ESLint directly. [1]\n\n### Fix options\n\n**Option A (recommended): upgrade ESLint to v9 and use flat config**\n```bash\nnpm i -D eslint@^9 eslint-config-next@^16\n```\nThen follow the Next.js flat-config example (`eslint.config.mjs` using `eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals`). [1]\n\n**Option B: stay on ESLint 8 by pinning Next/`eslint-config-next` to a pre-16 line**\n`eslint-config-next@15.1.6` declares compatibility with ESLint 8 (and 9) via peer deps, so this route typically avoids the v16/flat-config expectations. [2]\n\n### Why this mismatch shows up\nNext.js added ESLint 9 support during the Next.js 15 release cycle, and the ecosystem has been moving toward ESLint 9 as the baseline. [3]\n\n**Sources:** Next.js ESLint docs [1], `eslint-config-next@15.1.6` peer deps (UNPKG) [2], Next.js discussion noting ESLint 9 support timing [3].\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**ESLint 8 は eslint-config-next v16 と互換性がありません。アップグレードが必須です。**\n\n`eslint-config-next@16.1.6` は ESLint 9.0.0 以上をピア依存として要求しており、ESLint 8.x は明示的にサポートされていません。Next.js 16 は ESLint Flat Config (`eslint.config.mjs`) への移行を完了し、`next lint` コマンドも削除されました。この構成は ESLint 9 以降が必須です。\n\n**対応方法：**\n- **推奨:** ESLint を 9 にアップグレードし、Flat Config に移行してください（`npm i -D eslint@^9 eslint-config-next@^16`）\n- **代替案:** ESLint 8 を継続する場合、`eslint-config-next` を v15.x にダウングレードしてください\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@package.json` around lines 55 - 56, package.json currently pins \"eslint\":\n\"^8\" while \"eslint-config-next\": \"^16.1.6\" requires ESLint >=9; update\ndevDependencies so ESLint and Next's config match: either upgrade ESLint to ^9\nand adopt Next's Flat Config by replacing your legacy .eslintrc.* with\neslint.config.mjs and run npm i -D eslint@^9 eslint-config-next@^16, or\nalternatively keep ESLint 8 and downgrade eslint-config-next to a 15.x release\n(npm i -D eslint-config-next@^15) so the peer dependency aligns; modify\npackage.json devDependencies accordingly and reinstall.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits b33297c to c7fc0b2","created_at":"2026-03-09T15:40:59Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T01:25:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255054","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255054"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255054"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255054/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":55,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":56,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":44,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255070","pull_request_review_id":3916334651,"id":2906255070,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDONvrgrc6tOe7e","diff_hunk":"@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ export type CartItemWithProduct = Prisma.CartItemGetPayload<{\n }>;\n \n export type actionFunction = (\n-\tprevState: any,\n+\tprevState: { message: string },\n \tformData: FormData\n ) => Promise<{ message: string }>;","path":"utils/types.ts","commit_id":"f27220ad6e86838597f6c40637e4d585ffc8afe6","original_commit_id":"a2e66ac88626f39cced1ccb671e4d54703f58e2f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n**型の厳密化は良いですが、既存のアクションとの互換性を確認してください。**\n\n`prevState` の型を `any` から `{ message: string }` に変更することで型安全性が向上しますが、以下のアクション関数がこの型に適合していません：\n\n| アクション | 現在の prevState 型 |\n|----------|-------------------|\n| `deleteProductAction` | `{ productId: string }` |\n| `deleteReviewAction` | `{ reviewId: string }` |\n| `toggleFavoriteAction` | `{ productId, favoriteId, pathname }` |\n\nこれらのアクションは `FormContainer` 経由で使用されていますが、`.bind()` で異なるオブジェクトを渡しているため、型システム上は不整合が発生します。\n\n推奨される解決策：\n1. これらのアクションの ID を `formData` から取得するように変更する\n2. または、union 型でより柔軟な型定義にする\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>解決策1: formData を使用するパターン</summary>\n\n```typescript\n// 例: deleteProductAction を修正\nexport const deleteProductAction = async (\n  prevState: { message: string },\n  formData: FormData\n) => {\n  const productId = formData.get(\"productId\") as string;\n  // ... rest of implementation\n};\n\n// 呼び出し側 (hidden input を使用)\n<FormContainer action={deleteProductAction}>\n  <input type=\"hidden\" name=\"productId\" value={productId} />\n  <IconButton actionType=\"delete\" />\n</FormContainer>\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@utils/types.ts` around lines 7 - 10, The new actionFunction type in\nutils/types.ts restricts prevState to { message: string } but\ndeleteProductAction, deleteReviewAction and toggleFavoriteAction expect\ndifferent prevState shapes (they're bound via FormContainer/.bind), causing type\nincompatibility; either update those action functions (deleteProductAction,\ndeleteReviewAction, toggleFavoriteAction) to read identifiers from the provided\nFormData (e.g., use formData.get(\"...\") for\nproductId/reviewId/favoriteId/pathname) and keep prevState as { message: string\n}, or change actionFunction to accept a union/looser prevState type that covers\nthe existing shapes so current .bind usages remain valid—pick one approach and\napply it consistently across FormContainer-related actions.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-03-09T15:41:00Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T02:14:30Z","html_url":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255070","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255070"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pull/28#discussion_r2906255070"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/28"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/2906255070/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":7,"original_start_line":7,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":10,"original_line":10,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":7,"position":7,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myoshi2891/Next-Store/pulls/comments/3289881126","pull_request_review_id":4347236452,"id":3289881126,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDONvrgrc7EF5om","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@\n+import { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\n+import { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\n+import FormContainer from \"@/components/form/FormContainer\";\n+\n+// useToast のモック\n+vi.mock(\"@/hooks/use-toast\", () => ({\n+\tuseToast: () => ({ toast: vi.fn() }),\n+}));\n+\n+// useFormState / useActionState のモック（React バージョンに依存しないテスト）\n+vi.mock(\"react-dom\", async (importOriginal) => {\n+\tconst actual = await importOriginal<typeof import(\"react-dom\")>();\n+\treturn {\n+\t\t...actual,\n+\t\tuseFormState: (action: unknown, initialState: unknown) => [\n+\t\t\tinitialState,\n+\t\t\taction,\n+\t\t],\n+\t};\n+});\n+\n+vi.mock(\"react\", async (importOriginal) => {\n+\tconst actual = await importOriginal<typeof import(\"react\")>();\n+\treturn {\n+\t\t...actual,\n+\t\tuseActionState: (action: unknown, initialState: unknown) => [\n+\t\t\tinitialState,\n+\t\t\taction,\n+\t\t],\n+\t};\n+});","path":"__tests__/components/form/FormContainer.test.tsx","commit_id